reset: two NXP callers still pass the old (shared, optional, acquired) booleans
to of_reset_control_array_get().

Adapted from
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.90-91.xz

That level replaced those booleans with enum reset_control_flags, and the chain
applied it to the header while these two vendor drivers kept the four-argument
call. `(child, false, false, true)` means shared=no, optional=no, acquired=yes,
which the enum spells RESET_CONTROL_EXCLUSIVE; only the argument changes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/sec_mipi_dsim-imx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/sec_mipi_dsim-imx.c
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
 		if (!compat)
 			continue;
 
-		rstc = of_reset_control_array_get(child, false, false, true);
+		rstc = of_reset_control_array_get(child, RESET_CONTROL_EXCLUSIVE);
 		if (IS_ERR(rstc))
 			continue;
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/imx/lcdif/lcdif-common.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/imx/lcdif/lcdif-common.c
@@ -745,7 +745,7 @@
 		if (!compat)
 			continue;
 
-		rstc = of_reset_control_array_get(child, false, false, true);
+		rstc = of_reset_control_array_get(child, RESET_CONTROL_EXCLUSIVE);
 		if (IS_ERR(rstc))
 			continue;
 
